  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q3_Cabling
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: How far back may the pairs be untwisted at the plug in a Cat5e termination?
  choices:
  - No limit, as long as the colours are in order
  - "No more than 13 mm (\xBD inch)"
  - At least 50 mm, to make the plug easier to load
  - Exactly 25 mm on every conductor
  correctChoiceIndex: 1
  points: 10
  explanation: The twist is what cancels crosstalk. Untwisting more than about 13
    mm lets pairs interfere with each other, and the cable can fail certification
    even though a continuity tester shows all eight pins good.
